  "_comment": "Synthetic teaching-week fixture. NO real student data — fictional courses, teachers and rooms. Lesson dates are authored as dayOffset from 'now' and materialised to IS's compact YYYYMMDD by scripts/lib/fixtureRebase.ts, so this never rots. Ids are named after their offset (fx-d0-, fx-d7-, fx-dm7-) rather than a weekday, because which weekday an offset lands on depends on the day you run it. It spans three weeks on purpose: the phone's day switcher is the only way to reach another day, and an empty adjacent week hides whether it works. Serve with: npm run dev:web:week Day 0 deliberately carries one room of each resolution class, because the real-data snapshot is all-PEF and so can never exercise them: Q01 (building Q puts the hall code in `name`), A01 (buildings A/B/C/E/M put it in `nickname` — the case that was broken for every non-PEF faculty) and Z18 (a building the dataset carries no rooms for, so the map control must not be offered at all). Day 0 also carries a lesson that is RUNNING as you look at it (fx-d0-now) and the one after it (fx-d0-next), authored as startMinutesFromNow/endMinutesFromNow so \"TEĎ BĚŽÍ\", its countdown and the \"Pak:\" line are reachable at any hour.",
